learnings:
  - Derive who made a mark from the caller's class at the connection, not from the transport it arrived on
  - Ask what an upgrade does to state already on the user's machine before any contract id moves; the answer here was a release blocker nobody had planned for
  - A compatibility acceptance keyed on an exact content hash grants nothing and can be made to expire by test
  - Sequential worst cases need their own tests; random inserts hid a key-space exhaustion on the commonest action
  - Never find-and-replace an id across a spec that records its own history
